  "specId": "429df717-flow-help-contract",
  "issue": 521,
  "request": "Issue #521: Flow help is inconsistent with the actual argument contract. The parser definitions (args.flags, args.options, args.optionalOptions) and hand-written help diverge across all 67 FLOW_COMMANDS leaves: options are omitted from leaf help, group help shows unsupported --agent-work-dir, implicit -h/--help is absent, long subcommand names run into summaries, and declaration order controls display order. The cause is duplicated option/help authority and duplicated subcommand renderers in src/flow/registry.js, src/lib/dispatcher.js, src/lib/command-registry.js, and src/help.js. Extend the existing CommandDefinition with a dedicated option model for flags, required-value options, and optional-value options, compose target guards, runtime options, and implicit help from shared collections, project parser args and leaf/group help from that model, derive group options from the intersection of child leaf contracts, and consolidate sorting/alignment in one shared renderer reused by flow group help and help flow group. Preserve command execution semantics, target guard evaluation, and runtime directory behavior. Acceptance: every parser option plus implicit help appears exactly once in every leaf help; abort shows force, agent-work-dir, all five target guards, and -h/--help; get/set/report omit agent-work-dir while run shows it; every group row has visible separation; all groups sort subcommands by ascending name unless explicit display metadata overrides; both help entry points share ordering/layout; add registry/help contract tests for all leaves/groups including resume and prepare, plus focused E2E tests for abort, guarded get/set/run, long names, and ordering; do not change execution semantics or runtime directories. Target files: src/flow/registry.js, src/lib/dispatcher.js, src/lib/command-registry.js, src/help.js, tests/integration/lib/command-registry.test.js, tests/e2e/help.test.js.",
